## DE1 brief (owner-facing)

**Do this:** Dual-cap **single file** on `ooda/std/os/process.oo` (I1). Preferred process facades take `&ProcessCap`; hard residual facades keep `&SysCap`. Prove with dual-cap mains + facade-level deny that ProcessCap never reaches prctl/epoll/inotify (I2+I3). Do **not** touch emit (I4). Do **not** alias types (I6 PRUNE). Do **not** split `process_sys.oo` unless line pressure forces it (I5 HOLD). Leave async/python for a later residual wave (I7 HOLD / I11 WIN policy).

**Success =** ProcessCap-only main can `process_exec("true")`; ProcessCap-only main **cannot** call `process_prctl`; SysCap still supersedes preferred ops; G1–G6 floors green; no push until human gate.

**Out of scope this idea pack:** product code edits (Fairy = ideas only), domain SysCap bulk, seccomp, CAP-G7 format.

---

## Plain English

The process helpers still ask for the big OS key even when the small process key is enough. Best fix: one small file, two keys — spawn/exec with the small key, dangerous dials with the big key — plus tests that prove the small key never opens the dangerous dials. Pretending the two keys are the same is a security fail. Splitting more files or sweeping the whole library can wait.

---

*Fairy close: 11 ideas scored; ≥5 unique; DE1 winner = dual-cap single file; losers marked PRUNE. No product code. No push.*
